      "answer": "Based on my investigation of the codebase, here's what I found:\n\n## Current State\n\n**There is currently no built-in feature to see raw request bodies** sent to providers. The application:\n- Uses **Hono's `logger()` middleware** which only logs HTTP method, URL, and status\n- Makes provider API calls via `fetch()` without any request body logging\n- Has no debug environment variables for controlling request logging\n\n## How to Enable Request Body Logging\n\n### For Outgoing Requests to Providers (Claude, etc.):\n\nYou would need to modify the provider's `stream-fn.ts` files to add logging. For example, in `/apps/server/providers/src/claude/stream-fn.ts`, around line 241:\n\n```typescript\nconst response = await fetch(url, {\n  method: \"POST\",\n  headers,\n  body: JSON.stringify(body),\n  signal,\n});\n\n// Add this:\nconsole.log(\"Claude Request Body:\", body);\n```\n\n### For Incoming HTTP Requests to Console Server:\n\nAdd a custom middleware to `/apps/server/api/src/app.ts` to capture and log request bodies:\n\n```typescript\napp.use(\"*\", async (c, next) =\u003e {\n  const body = await c.req.text();\n  if (body \u0026\u0026 process.env.DEBUG_REQUESTS) {\n    console.log(`${c.req.method} ${c.req.path}:`, body);\n  }\n  // Re-create the request body for the handler\n  c.env.rawBody = body;\n  await next();\n});\n```\n\nThen enable it with: `DEBUG_REQUESTS=true`\n\n## Recommendation\n\nIf you want to see what's being sent to Claude/providers right now, the quickest approach is to add `console.log` statements directly in the provider files and **restart the server**. Would you like me to implement this for a specific provider?"
